## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a secure, end-to-end streaming pipeline with encryption, data redaction, and reliable error handling.

## Key Concepts
- AWS KMS and the AWS Encryption SDK for per-record encryption
- PII data redaction techniques
- Parquet format in S3 with date-based partitioning
- Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) design and routing patterns
- X-Ray distributed tracing across producer, validator, and sink services
- LocalStack for local testing and development

## Code Example
```javascript
// Decrypt and process Kinesis record
const decrypted = encryptionClient.decrypt(encryptedPayload, dataKey);

// Validate telemetry schema
if (!schemaValidator.validate(decrypted)) {
  await dlqClient.send(JSON.stringify(decrypted));
  return;
}

// Redact PII fields
const redacted = piiRedactor.redact(decrypted);

// Write to S3 as partitioned Parquet
await s3Client.putObject({
  Bucket: 'telemetry-bucket',
  Key: `year=${date.getFullYear()}/month=${date.getMonth()}/day=${date.getDate()}/${uuid()}.parquet`,
  Body: await parquetWriter.write(redacted)
});
```

